  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic empowerment</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARQ Capital, an SME-focused investor, is implementing an innovative product with IW&#x2019;s support, to give women-owned and -led businesses access to growth capital in the Philippines. 
&#x200d;
SheSecure is an investment product which applies a gender lens to support the growth capital needs of women-owned and -led small businesses. SheSecure offers capped loans together with interest rate reductions for investees that are tied to improvements in gender equality practices. These funds can be utilised by the enterprises to fuel expansion, invest in new technologies, or support their working capital requirements.  
&#x200d;
SheSecure tackles two critical gaps faced by larger women-owned and -led small businesses in the Philippines &#x2013; the lack of appropriate capital and the need for strategic business support. By providing incentives linked to measurable progress in gender performance, SheSecure also empowers companies to mainstream gender equality&#x2014;ensuring opportunities and leadership roles are accessible to everyone, regardless of gender.
&#x200d;
&#x201c;Our goal with SheSecure is to nurture growth-oriented businesses that meet gender-lens criteria while encouraging more companies to adopt gender-inclusive practices,&#x201d; said Abigail Tan, ARQ SME BDC Managing Partner. &#x201c;By prioritizing both profit and social progress, we create a win-win for businesses, their customers, and society as a whole.&#x201d;</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the Philippines, 33 companies received support to strengthen their internal systems for advancing WGE policy advocacy and capacity building for HR and management teams. This led to stronger accountability systems and measurable change with participating companies demonstrating more sustained approaches to WGE. 
&#x200d;
Investing in Women also works with credible local institutions to strengthen the evidence base and drive collective action needed to influence and inform policy reform that supports women&#x2019;s equal economic participation. As part of its research partnership with Investing in Women, the Australian National University&#x2019;s Global Institute for Women&#x2019;s Leadership delivered the Comparative Study on  Gender-Inclusive Part-time Work Policies which was considered by the Department of Economy, Planning and Development (DepDEV) in drafting of the Government of Philippines&#x2019; Trabaho Para sa Bayan Plan 2025-34.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic empowerment</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing in Women commenced a partnership with Terratai in 2024-25 to seed fund its investment window, offering long-term, fit-for-purpose capital to early-stage women-led nature-based solutions (NBS) businesses across Indonesia.
&#x200d;
Terratai is dedicated to growing early-stage ventures into sustainable companies that can help nature to recover and thrive. Drawing on a deep familiarity with the Asian venture landscape, Terratai&#x2019;s blended finance facility will de-risk investments into innovative and early-stage women-led companies by providing long term, customised venture building support  to their portfolio companies, to aid in their expansion and economic resilience. 
&#x200d;
Terratai has identified that women-led businesses in Indonesia struggle to raise investment and to reach scale &#x2013; and for nature focused companies this bar is even higher. The partnership with IW will accelerate Terratai&#x2019;s investment in women-led companies that are working to protect and restore Indonesia&#x2019;s most at-risk land and seascapes.
&#x200d;
Through the partnership with investing in Women, Terratai is investing in HANDEP (Handmade Ethical Products) &#x2013; a social enterprise working with Indigenous Dayak women rattan artisans in Central Kalimantan. HANDEP partners with these artisans to support women&#x2019;s leadership, sustainable livelihoods and forest conservation.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Together for Good initiative&#x2014;led by Good Return, a non-profit organisation focused on women&#x2019;s economic empowerment in the Asia-Pacific region and APPEND Inc. (Alliance of Philippine Partners in Enterprise Development), with funding from Investing in Women&#x2014;aims to build a gender-equal and socially inclusive microfinance sector in the Philippines. The initiative uses campaigns to promote equitable norms around care and economic roles, while building a Community of Practice (CoP) comprised of staff from microfinance institutions (MFIs) who actively support gender equality, serving as a peer network to drive gender-transformative change within their institutions.
&#x200d;
To date, seven MFIs from the APPEND network were supported to develop gender action plans, informed by qualitative research carried out within the MFIs. 
&#x200d;
Good Return organised the National Gender Advocates Conference in April 2024, which brought together field staff and branch leaders. As a result, 31 participants joined the CoP and began leading peer dialogues within their organisations on equal sharing of care and economic roles in households.
&#x200d;
This initiative has the potential for spillover effects. MFI staff interact with clients and households daily and are seen as trusted advisors, enabling them to support how households negotiate care and economic roles.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through Investing in Women, Australia supported business coalitions and partners in the Philippines, Indonesia, Vietnam and Myanmar to advance workplace gender equality. Business coalitions help employers create a fairer workplace, attract and retain diverse teams, and deliver on their environmental, social and governance strategies. The initiative supported businesses to apply Workplace Gender Equality (WGE) tools and market knowledge to help leaders benchmark their business, make more informed decisions, and embed gender equality into workplace culture and operations. 
&#x200d;
In Indonesia, Australia worked with 37 companies to embed WGE considerations in day-to-day operations by facilitating regular policy reviews and working closely with senior leaders and promoting flexible work arrangements. As a result, several companies implemented more inclusive HR practices and are progressing toward their gender equality priorities. The business coalition also provided technical assistance to Godrej in launching an on-site daycare facility at its headquarters. The Indonesian Minister of Women&#x2019;s Empowerment and Child Protection called it a model for family-supportive workplaces aligned with the 2024 Maternal and Child Protection Law.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
